+/*
+  A test driver for the Qt client, for screenshots and click checks on a
+  Mac where scripted input from outside the process is not allowed.
+
+  FREECIV_UI_DRIVE=<script> starts it; FREECIV_UI_DRIVE_OUT=<dir> is where
+  shots and drive.log go (default: the current directory). It waits for a
+  running game with a focus unit, then runs one line of the script every
+  "pace" milliseconds. Input goes through QTest, so Qt's own enter, leave,
+  hover and tooltip handling runs as for a real mouse.
+
+    pace MS                 delay between lines (default 900)
+    wait MS                 extra delay
+    hover portrait|chip N|action TEXT|button TEXT|label TEXT|tip TEXT
+    click portrait|chip N|action TEXT|button TEXT|label TEXT|tip TEXT [shift]
+    rclick ...              the same with the right button
+    wheel DELTA tip TEXT    a wheel step of DELTA (120 a notch up, -120 down)
+                            on the button whose tooltip contains TEXT
+                            (button: any visible button in the window whose
+                            text contains TEXT; label: a visible label whose
+                            text is TEXT; tip: any visible button whose
+                            tooltip contains TEXT, for icon-only buttons)
+    city NAME               where the city is, its build, stock and gold
+    chooser ROW COL         pick that cell of the open production chooser,
+                            as a click on it does (selection changed)
+    accept                  accept the active modal box (its OK button)
+    endturn                 end the turn, as the Turn Done button does
+    key K                   g f s w space escape enter shift+enter, or one
+                            letter
+    research NAME           research the advance NAME (its rule name)
+    opencity NAME           open the own city NAME, as a click on it does
+    scroll DX DY            move the map origin by DX, DY canvas pixels
+    drag X Y DX DY          left drag through the window from X, Y (window
+                            points) by DX, DY, in eight moves
+    drag unit DX DY         the same from the focus unit's tile
+    mapwheel DX DY [notch]  a two-finger trackpad scroll of DX, DY points
+                            on the map, or a mouse wheel angle with notch
+    pointer X Y             leave the pointer at X, Y (map points; off
+                            the map if negative or past its size) and
+                            log the map's origin
+    clicktile DX DY         left click the tile DX, DY from the focus unit
+                            (through action_button_pressed, which the map's
+                            mouse release calls, since that reads QCursor)
+    option [NAME] on|off    a boolean client option through its callback
+                            (default gui_qt_freeciv45_panels)
+    chat TEXT               send a chat line or a /command to the server
+    dismiss                 close the modal boxes (welcome message...)
+                            and an open popup menu
+    unit ID                 where unit ID is, its activity and orders
+    page main               show the start page (before a shot of it)
+    state LABEL             append the state to drive.log (with the
+                            window title)
+    shot NAME               state, then NAME.png of the window (+ tooltip)
+    quit
+*/
